// BUGS #128 guard: the left side of a compound assignment must be a place.
//
// `+=` desugars in the parser to `target = target + (rhs)`, so a target that is
// not assignable produces `5 = 5 + 1` — an Assign node over a literal. Without
// this guard that shape reaches the checker, which reports it in terms of the
// synthesized assignment rather than the `+=` the user wrote, or (worse, given
// `build_assign`'s fallthrough) is quietly turned back into a bare ExprStmt and
// the whole line vanishes with no diagnostic at all. A statement that silently
// does nothing is the failure mode this file exists to prevent.
//
// The four assignable shapes are a variable, `obj.field`, `this.field` and
// `obj[i]`; all four are exercised in test/pass/increment.sf. Anything else — a
// literal, a call result, an arithmetic expression — is rejected here by name.
//
// The same check backs postfix `++`, with the wording adjusted for a single
// operand; see test/fail/prefix_increment.sf.
//
// Expected: "the left side of '+=' must be a variable, field or element" and
// exit 1.

var a: Int = 1
5 += 1
IO.println(a)
